+	 *
+	 *     53 ms per frame is 19 per second at best, and the viewfinder
+	 *     stutters. At 2592x1940 there are four times fewer pixels.
+	 *
+	 *   DARKNESS. The 5 MP one comes from a 2x2 binning, that is four times
+	 *     more light per pixel. Measured with the same scene and the same
+	 *     exposure, the median over the black pedestal (64) was ~6
+	 *     times higher in the binned one.
+	 *
+	 * That is, the big mode gives less image and costs four times more.
+	 * It will be restored when there is hardware demosaicing or some way to
+	 * hint to libcamera which mode to use for the viewfinder.
+	 *
+	 *	{
+	 *		.width = 5184,
+	 *		.height = 3880,
+	 *		.hts = 5440,
+	 *		.vts = 4160,
+	 *		.exposure = 512,
+	 *		.reg_list = {
